  "label": "Black Lives Matter is mapped onto Black men in prison uniforms carrying sacks",
  "description": "The top text 'black lives matter' is juxtaposed with the visual of Black men in prison uniforms carrying sacks, creating an analogical mapping where the phrase 'black lives matter' is implicitly mapped onto the visual representation of Black men in prison. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it uses the image of incarcerated Black men to imply that Black lives do not matter, thereby mocking the movement. The mapping is established through direct visual-textual juxtaposition, where the text 'black lives matter' is positioned above the image of the prisoners, creating a direct association between the phrase and the visual material.",
